  "question": "Find the area enclosed between the curves $y=\\sin x$ and $y=\\cos x$ for $x\\in[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}]$.",
  "answeroption": "D",
  "explanation": "Intersection at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Split the integral:<br /><br />$A=\\int_{0}^{\\pi/4}(\\cos x-\\sin x)dx + \\int_{\\pi/4}^{\\pi/2}(\\sin x-\\cos x)dx = 2\\sqrt{2}-2$.<br /><br />Thus required area $=2\\sqrt{2}-2$.",
